  "result": "I fixed the paging bug in `src/server/repositories/_paging.ts`, but I haven't run the tests or walked any list page by page.\n\nThe cause was `keysetPredicate`, which resumed after the last row shown with `sortColumn < cursor.sortValue` only. Rows that share the cursor's timestamp were skipped, and a bulk import or a burst of notifications stamps every row with the same timestamp.\n\nIt now resumes with `sortColumn < v OR (sortColumn = v AND id < cursor.id)`, which matches the existing `ORDER BY sort DESC, id DESC`. That gives every entry exactly once, in the same order as one large page. The same helper backs issues, notifications, activity, projects, members, comments and search, so all of those lists are fixed together.\n\nEvery one of those queries already filters on the org, so pages shouldn't include another workspace's entries. I didn't change any of that.",
